      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case report is presented that deals with mental nerve paresthesia resulting from the \"flare-up\" of a mandibular second premolar with three root canals. A review of the literature and discussion follow, which suggest possible mechanisms that may be responsible for paresthesia as well as treatment regimens that may be used to minimize the incidence of this unexpected but occasional post-treatment endodontic sequela."},
